te with its assumptions, never a guaranteed burn duration. Heat probes receive actual time-varying local exposure, not a magic heating flag.\\\\nControl and safety: tending may add explicitly charged fuel, separate burning pieces with a real suitable tool, or reduce air using a physically adequate cover. It cannot set an arbitrary temperature. Quenching needs acquired water or other proven suitable material in sufficient quantity and an actual delivery method; smothering needs a real suitable cover or adequate noncombustible covering material. Consume/translocate those inputs and model cooling or oxygen exclusion. Ordinary nearby soil alone does not imply gathered extinguishing stock. Before ignition require an executable extinguishing option and inspect the reachable surroundings for exposed combustibles; this reduces risk but grants no safety immunity. Heat exposure can burn actors, ignite represented susceptible nearby material, or leave dangerous embers according to the same rules. If a compatible spread/hazard model is absent, that is a blocking dependency, not permission to run consequence-free fire. Extinguishing success requires observable absence of combustion and an explicit residual-temperature reading; flames disappearing alone may leave hot embers.\\\\nA lit source is a persistent world process that burns each simulation step without continued commands until fuel/oxygen is exhausted or actual extinguishing succeeds. It needs replenished fuel and periodic observation for continued controlled use; no indefinite output. Leaving, cancelling, interruption or death does not switch it off. Active work stops on loss of reach, incapacity, insufficient energy, cancellation or death. Save completed friction work and input changes; retained heat still cools through ordinary simulation, so resuming does not preserve stale ignition progress. Release surviving reserved inputs once on cancellation; consumed fuel, effort, wear and elapsed time are never refunded. Death 