d decay in code rather than repeated model review.\\\",\\\"visualReview\\\":\\\"Use reusable metadata linked to a persistent source ID, location, footprint, fuel quantity, active mode, work progress, flame intensity, smoke, ember state, exposed temperature, residue and hazard radius. Emit observable events for friction contact, measured heating, verified ignition, fuel addition, quench/smother actions, flame-out and verified cooling, with input/output object references and evidence timestamps. Render flame only when combustion actually begins; smoke and embers require their corresponding physical states. A failed attempt may show movement, wear or measured warming, never a successful fire, extinguished-safe badge or heating success. Hot remains remain visually distinct from verified cold residue. Visual effects do not independently grant functional heat, experience or knowledge; measurements and uncertainty remain separate from presentation.\\\"}]}\"}","annotations":[],"logprobs":[]}}

